Chapter 4: Network Devices

This is one of the most important chapters in networking because these are the physical devices that make communication possible.

If you understand this chapter thoroughly, you will be able to answer many networking interview questions and understand how data moves through a network.

What Are Network Devices?

A network device is a hardware component that helps connect devices, forward data, improve communication, or provide security.

Think of a city:

Roads → Network cables
Traffic signals → Switches
Highways → Routers
Security checkpoints → Firewalls

Without these, transportation would be chaotic. Similarly, without network devices, computers cannot communicate efficiently.

